plugins/vox - notices for the VOX package (vox.trombone, vox.a64.rmp)

VOX's DSP is Pink Trombone's (the Glottis and Tract objects and the tongue / constriction shaping of TractUI), ported
to C for one voice a state and adapted for the Sidecar (vox.c's header lists the changes: knobs for the touches, an
envelope for the glottis's intensity, the note as the pitch, 32-bit floats, recurrences for the LF waveform, a
release to exact silence).
  Taken from:  https://dood.al/pinktrombone/  (index.html, "Pink Trombone, version 1.1, March 2017, by Neil Thapen";
               fetched 2026-10-30, SHA-256 94f92caa426e9e7bd928ab82c7d0d75d297e1090411867f62dd09081f4e1cec2;
               the original page has no repository commit)
  Licence:     MIT, Copyright 2017 Neil Thapen (LICENSE.pinktrombone: the licence text from index.html's header
               comment, unchanged but for trailing spaces)
No upstream file is in this repository or the package: vox.c is a rewrite of the DSP in C.

The adaptation and the glue (vox.c, manifest.json, the Makefile, tests/): MIT, Copyright 2026 trigcondition and
contributors (LICENSE). The package links sdk/rmp/shim (MIT).
